---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '../config/site';
---

<Layout title="Privacy Policy">
  <article class="container legal-page">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p><strong>Last updated: October 17, 2026</strong></p>

    <h2>1. Data Controller</h2>
    <p>The controller responsible for processing personal data on this website is:</p>
    <p>
      <strong>{siteConfig.name}</strong><br />
      Email: <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.email}`}>{siteConfig.email}</a><br />
      Website: <a href={siteConfig.url}>{siteConfig.url}</a><br />
      Postal address: see the <a href="/imprint">Imprint</a>
    </p>

    <h2>2. General Information</h2>
    <p>
      I take the protection of your personal data seriously. This Privacy Policy explains what
      information may be collected when you visit this website, why it is processed, and what rights
      you have under the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) and applicable German data
      protection laws.
    </p>
    <p>Personal data is any information that can be used to identify you directly or indirectly.</p>
    <p>
      You are not required to provide any personal data to browse this website. Providing data is
      only necessary if you contact me or book a call. I do not use automated decision-making or
      profiling.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Website Hosting</h2>
    <p>
      This website is built with Astro and hosted by a third-party hosting provider. When you visit
      the website, technical information may automatically be collected in server log files. This
      may include:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>IP address</li>
      <li>Date and time of access</li>
      <li>Requested pages or files</li>
      <li>Browser type and version</li>
      <li>Operating system</li>
      <li>Referring URL</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      This information is processed to deliver the website, maintain its security, and troubleshoot
      technical problems. The legal basis for this processing is Article 6(1)(f) GDPR, based on the
      legitimate interest in providing a secure and reliable website.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Hosting provider:</strong> [INSERT HOSTING PROVIDER NAME AND ADDRESS]. A data
      processing agreement is in place with the provider where required. Server log data is deleted
      or anonymised after a short period, generally within a few days to weeks, depending on the
      provider's settings.
    </p>
    <p>
      If the hosting provider is located outside the EU/EEA, data may be transferred to a third
      country. Such transfers are based on an adequacy decision or on standard contractual clauses
      of the European Commission. For further information, please consult the provider's privacy
      policy.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Fonts</h2>
    <p>
      The fonts used on this website are hosted locally on the website's own server. Your browser
      does not connect to Google or any other third party to load them, so no data is transmitted
      to external font providers.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Google Search Console (only with your consent)</h2>
    <p>
      This website uses Google Search Console to monitor its visibility in Google Search and
      understand its search performance. The service provides information about search queries,
      clicks, impressions, and indexing. This information helps me understand how the website
      appears in search results and identify technical issues.
    </p>
    <p>
      To prove ownership of this website to Google, a verification tag
      (<code>google-site-verification</code>) is added to the page source. This tag is only added
      after you consent in the cookie banner; without consent it is not present. Google's systems
      may process technical data such as your IP address when they access the website, so I only
      enable the tag with your consent.
    </p>
    <p>
      The legal basis is your consent under Article 6(1)(a) GDPR and § 25(1) TDDDG. You can withdraw
      consent at any time through "Cookie settings" in the footer. Search Console only provides me
      with aggregated information about search performance, not data about individual visitors.
    </p>
    <p>
      Google Search Console is a website management tool. Using it does not, by itself, mean that
      Google Analytics is installed or that visitors are being tracked through Google Analytics.
      Further information is available in
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google's Privacy Policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Contact by Email</h2>
    <p>
      If you contact me by email, I process the information you provide, including your email
      address, name if provided, and the contents of your message. This information is used to
      respond to your enquiry and handle any subsequent communication.
    </p>
    <p>
      The legal basis for processing is Article 6(1)(b) GDPR when your enquiry relates to a contract
      or steps taken before entering into a contract. For other enquiries, processing may be based
      on Article 6(1)(f) GDPR, where applicable.
    </p>
    <p>
      Your information will be retained only for as long as necessary to handle your enquiry and
      fulfil any applicable legal obligations (for example, statutory retention periods for business
      correspondence). It is not shared with third parties except my email provider, which processes
      messages on my behalf.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Booking a Call (Cal.com, only with your consent)</h2>
    <p>
      You can book a 15-minute call through a calendar provided by Cal.com. The calendar is only
      loaded after you consent in the cookie banner. When it loads, your browser connects to
      Cal.com servers, which receive your IP address and browser information. If you then book a
      slot, the details you enter (such as name, email address and message) are processed by
      Cal.com to arrange the appointment. Without consent, the calendar is not loaded. Cal.com may
      process data in the United States or other third countries; transfers rely on the provider's
      safeguards such as standard contractual clauses. Booking data is kept only as long as needed to
      handle the appointment and any follow-up.
    </p>
    <p>
      The legal basis for loading the calendar is your consent under Article 6(1)(a) GDPR and § 25(1)
      TDDDG; for processing a booking it is Article 6(1)(b) GDPR. You can withdraw consent at any
      time through "Cookie settings" in the footer. See the
      <a href="https://cal.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Cal.com Privacy Policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Social Media Links</h2>
    <p>
      This website contains links to my profiles on social media platforms, including Instagram,
      TikTok and YouTube. The website uses ordinary links rather than embedded social media feeds or
      video players. Clicking a link redirects you to the relevant platform.
    </p>
    <p>
      Once you visit an external platform, that platform may collect and process personal data in
      accordance with its own privacy policy. I have no control over how these platforms process
      your information. You can find further information here:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="https://help.instagram.com/519522125107875" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Instagram Privacy Policy</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://www.tiktok.com/legal/page/eea/privacy-policy/en" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">TikTok Privacy Policy</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Privacy Policy, including YouTube</a></li>
    </ul>

    <h2>9. Cookies, Local Storage and Tracking Technologies</h2>
    <p>
      This website does not use Google Analytics, advertising cookies, or other analytics or
      tracking tools. The website's hosting provider may process information necessary to deliver
      and secure the website (see Section 3).
    </p>
    <p>
      When you make a choice in the cookie banner, it is stored in your browser's local storage
      (key: <code>site-consent-v1</code>) so that you are not asked again. This is strictly necessary
      to respect your choice and does not require consent. The optional services (Google
      Search Console verification and the Cal.com booking calendar) are only activated if you consent. You can change or withdraw your choice at any
      time via "Cookie settings" in the footer.
    </p>
    <p>
      If additional services, cookies, or tracking technologies are introduced in the future, this
      Privacy Policy will be updated accordingly and consent will be obtained before activating them.
    </p>

    <h2>10. Recipients of Your Data</h2>
    <p>
      Your personal data is only passed on to the service providers named in this policy, namely the
      hosting provider, Google (Search Console), Cal.com (bookings) and my email provider,
      and only to the extent described. I do not sell your data.
    </p>

    <h2>11. External Websites</h2>
    <p>
      This website may contain links to third-party websites and services, including social media
      platforms and external resources. When you follow these links, the privacy policies of those
      third parties apply to your subsequent activity. I am not responsible for the content or data
      protection practices of external websites.
    </p>

    <h2>12. Your Rights Under the GDPR</h2>
    <p>Under the GDPR, you may have the right to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Access:</strong> Request information about the personal data processed about you.</li>
      <li><strong>Rectification:</strong> Request correction of inaccurate or incomplete personal data.</li>
      <li><strong>Erasure:</strong> Request deletion of your personal data where the legal requirements are met.</li>
      <li><strong>Restriction:</strong> Request restriction of certain processing activities.</li>
      <li><strong>Objection:</strong> Object to processing based on legitimate interests where applicable.</li>
      <li><strong>Data portability:</strong> Receive certain personal data in a structured, commonly used format.</li>
      <li><strong>Withdraw consent:</strong> Withdraw consent at any time when processing is based on consent. Withdrawal does not affect the lawfulness of processing before withdrawal.</li>
      <li><strong>Lodge a complaint:</strong> Submit a complaint to a competent data protection supervisory authority, for example the authority of your place of residence or workplace.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      To exercise your rights, contact me using the email address provided in Section 1. If you are
      based in Germany, you can also contact the competent data protection supervisory authority for
      your federal state.
    </p>

    <h2>13. Data Security</h2>
    <p>
      I take reasonable technical and organisational measures to protect personal data against
      accidental loss, unauthorised access, alteration, or disclosure. However, no method of
      transmitting or storing information online can guarantee absolute security.
    </p>

    <h2>14. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
    <p>
      This Privacy Policy may be updated to reflect changes to the website, the services used, or
      applicable legal requirements. The current version will be published on this page, together
      with the date of the latest update.
    </p>
  </article>
</Layout>
